# unit-watch-apocalypse.vrs: unit-watch D26 (Session 2), apocalypse horde units and roamers in game. apo-test
# (tools/vrclient/fixtures/apo-test.json: Faction_Undead, CHAR_Undead_Guardian -1967480038 and
# CHAR_Undead_GhostMilitia_Light -1618703048, 2 hotspots 300 m or more apart, 3 roamers each, 2 hordes from 1 min, size 8,
# marchSpeed 3.0) is started with Chaos at the wait spot; once horde 1 has risen Chaos goes to the far spot W, 150 m beyond
# hotspot 2 on the line from hotspot 1, and marks every live unit with `.nyar event unstick apo-test` (A3: a unit sunk by a
# dev write does not stay sunk). "stuck: … (admin)" and "recovered: …" follow for a Guardian and a Ghost Militia, and
# with every unit marked no unmarked mate is left to land beside, so they land 50-60 m from Chaos and `.nyar debug here
# 70` at W lists them (landing beside its horde is D5's unit test and the test weekend's). With no fight, each try fails after StuckSeconds and "removed: … no kill credit" follows; no
# "apocalypse apo-test spread" line follows (a removal is a despawn: no death, no spread).
# Restart (by hand, after this scenario; logs copied first, D26): the next boot logs "event apo-test resumed after restart
# (horde <k>/2, <u> units to rebuild)" with u not counting the removed unit (compare with `.nyar event info apo-test`
# before the restart, shot uw-apo-before-restart).
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with unit-watch step 3; apo-test (fixture above) enabled, every other spawning definition disabled;
# [UnitWatch] Enabled = true, StuckSeconds 90, StallMinutes 10; NyarDevTools (.devtp) and DevChatEcho; vrclient
# with `calc` and `expect-calc`; no purge cooldown; Chaos invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false;
# set again after every teleport, as a death resets it).
# Run: --var WX=-1690 --var WZ=-1400 (the wait spot, 300 m or more from both hotspots, as apocalypse.vrs)
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${WX} ${WZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test hotspots: 2 \( timeout=10
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )hotspot 1: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<H1X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<H1Z>-?[0-9]+) \\n hotspot 2: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<H2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<H2Z>-?[0-9]+) timeout=10
calc D12 = hypot(${H2X} - ${H1X}, ${H2Z} - ${H1Z})
calc WFX = round(${H2X} + 150 * (${H2X} - ${H1X}) / ${D12})
calc WFZ = round(${H2Z} + 150 * (${H2Z} - ${H1Z}) / ${D12})
expect-seen apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
# A. every live unit marked from W (A3: a sunk unit does not stay sunk, so `.nyar event unstick` makes the marks)
chat .devtp ${WFX} ${WFZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<QX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<QZ>-?[0-9.]+)
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event unstick apo-test
expect-reply units marked
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch apo-test stuck: CHAR_Undead_Guardian wave [0-9]+ \(admin\) timeout=10
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch apo-test recovered: CHAR_Undead_Guardian try 1/2, [0-9]+ m \((group|player|anchor)\) timeout=20
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch apo-test recovered: CHAR_Undead_GhostMilitia_Light try 1/2, [0-9]+ m \((group|player|anchor)\) timeout=20
# B. where they landed: every unit is marked, so no unmarked mate is left to land beside and each lands 50-60 m from the
# nearest player, Chaos at W (D5's order: group, player, anchor); landing beside its horde is D5's unit test and the
# test weekend's (A3)
wait 5
chat .nyar debug here 70
expect-reply apo-test
shot full uw-apo-recovered
# C. at W: no fight, so each try fails after StuckSeconds (try 2 "(seen)", Chaos beside them) and the units are removed
# with no kill credit, in view after their wait, and no spread
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch apo-test removed: CHAR_Undead_Guardian wave [0-9]+ after 2 tries, no kill credit timeout=330
expect-no-log apocalypse apo-test spread timeout=15
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-reply removed
shot full uw-apo-before-restart
# left running for the restart (by hand, logs copied first): the next boot's resumed line is read from its log
